  "output": "\n\nNo Phoenix or hotel emails in the inbox — let me check your calendar for the Phoenix dates to anchor the email.\n\nFound the earlier drafts — this thread has history. There are actually three placeholder versions of this dispute email sitting in the drafts folder from earlier attempts. I'll consolidate onto the best one, add the accountant BCC per your standing rule, and file it for approval.\n\nThe accountant BCC address on file is a non-deliverable placeholder (it fails validation), so I'll flag that instead of baking in a dead address. Filing the draft for approval now.\n\nDone — the dispute email is waiting in Needs-you (it was already queued from earlier, now it's the single authoritative version; I left the two older placeholder copies in drafts to ignore or delete).\n\nBefore it can send, fill in: hotel name + front-desk email, both charge amounts and posting dates, confirmation number, stay dates, and your card's last 4. I couldn't find any of those in your inbox or calendar — travel confirmations live in your personal Gmail — so they're all bracketed.\n\nTwo flags on the card side:\n\n1. Dispute the SECOND of the two identical charges with your issuer (the earlier one is the valid stay charge). If one of them is actually a pending authorization hold rather than a posted charge, wait 3-5 business days — holds often drop off on their own, and disputing a hold that was never billed muddies the claim.\n2. Give the hotel 5-7 business days to reverse it before filing — the email says exactly that, which strengthens the dispute if it comes to that.\n\nOne blocker to know: your accountant BCC (receipts@my-accountant-domain) is still a placeholder that won't deliver, so it's not on this draft. Send me the real address once and I'll bake it into every invoice email going forward.",
